  "verbalization": "Isopropyl caprate appears to interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a multi-step pathway involving the DNMT3A2/3L complex. The evidence suggests that Isopropyl caprate targets this complex, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Robustadial B, Chlorajapolide E, and 2,4-Dinitrophenol. These compounds are all known to modulate the activity of glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, indicating a potential mechanism by which Isopropyl caprate may influence the enzyme's function. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Isopropyl caprate in modulating the activity of the DNMT3A2/3L complex, which could, in turn, affect glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. The evidence supports a relationship where Isopropyl caprate acts as a modulator of the DNMT3A2/3L complex, which is a known target of several compounds that influence glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase. This suggests a potential regulatory role for Isopropyl caprate in the metabolic processes involving this enzyme.",
